 Systems of Linear Equations:
 is more than one linear equation on the same graph. basically we have 3 types of graphs:
 -2 lines that cross each other at some point: that one has one solution where the 2 lines interesct.
 -2 parallel lines: no solution as there is no common point
 -2 lines that are on top of each other or the same: that one has an infinte no of solutions since they interesect at every point.

 NOTE: what we are mainly looking for is a point where these 2 lines cross or intersect.

